{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-52730",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "By the segment addition postulate, we have\n\n$$\nAD=AB+BC+CD.\n$$\n\nTo solve for $x,$ we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\nAD=17,\\,AB=x-2,\\,BC=9,\\,CD=2x-5,\n$$\n\n \n\nand then solve the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =AB+BC+CD \\\\ 17 & =(x-2)+9+(2x-5) \\\\ 17 & =3x+2 \\\\ 3x & =15 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
